hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"342","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him): In the year of the conquest of Makkah, I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he saw a man having cupping done on the eighteenth of Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), while holding my hand, said, ""The fast of the one who does cupping and the one who gets cupped is broken."
"343","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that ""The one who gives cupping and the one who gets cupped, their fast is broken."
"344","Maqsam (may Allah have mercy on him), the freed slave of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done while fasting and in the state of ihram."
